diff --git a/.changeset/listen-extensions.md b/.changeset/listen-extensions.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5e4330e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/listen-extensions.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+---
+'@modelcontextprotocol/server': minor
+---
+
+`createMcpHandler` and `serveStdio` accept `listenExtensions`, so an extension can honor its own fields of the `subscriptions/listen` filter (for example the Tasks extension's `taskIds`) and deliver its notifications on listen streams, while the entry keeps owning ack-first, subscription-ID stamping, keepalive, subscription limits and teardown.
+
+- A `ListenExtension` declares its notification `methods`, `honor(requested, capabilities)` returning the fields it honors from the raw requested filter, `accepts(honored, event)`, and an optional `validate(requested)` that rejects a malformed field with `-32602`.
+- The core filter is honored first against the server's capabilities; an extension cannot add a core field.
+- If `honor()` throws, the ack and the subscription record both leave out that extension's fields, the error is reported through `onerror`, and the core subscription is served as usual.
+- `ServerEvent` gains `{ kind: 'extension'; method; params? }`, published with `handler.notify.extension(method, params)`. On `serveStdio`, an instance's notification whose method an extension declares is routed per subscription and dropped when none accepts it.
+
+New exported types: `ListenExtension`, `ExtensionServerEvent`. `ServerNotifier` gains `extension()`; code that implements `ServerNotifier` itself must add it.
diff --git a/.changeset/request-scoped-listen.md b/.changeset/request-scoped-listen.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..948fd941
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/request-scoped-listen.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+---
+'@modelcontextprotocol/client': minor
+'@modelcontextprotocol/server': minor
+---
+
+Preserve extension fields in acknowledged listen filters. Add request-scoped
+async `ListenExtension.open` with source publication, cancellation and disposal
+on the existing HTTP/stdio subscription lifetime. Source setup cannot block stdio
+cancellation or deliver before the acknowledged filter.
+
+EOF cancels pending and active sources. Post-acknowledgment output is bounded on
+HTTP and stdio, and cancelled subscriptions cannot emit previously queued output.
+Preserve class-based extension identity and settle blocked stdio writes on close.
+
+Add a stream-scoped client receiver to avoid mixing overlapping filters, and
+let an asynchronous source close its own existing subscription on source loss.
+Late or unknown addressed data frames never fall back to global handlers.
+Synchronous and asynchronous receiver failures close only their subscription.
+Preserve typed protocol errors from source setup. Add source `finish()` so final
+notifications survive acknowledgment and bounded stdio queues; caller cancellation
+continues to discard queued output.
